To suggest additional VODS for the website you can do one of the following:
<ul class="submitBullets">
    <li>
        You can create an <a href ="https://github.com/WhiteTPoison/projectplusvods/issues/new" rel="noopener noreferrer">issue on the project GitHub page</a> and we'll add the VODS for you.
        <ul>
            <li>
             <u><b>VODS must contain one of the following forms of metadata:</u></b>
            </li>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Separate and properly titled videos including:
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            The title of the event
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Names of both players
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Both respective characters (if a player used more than one, list them all)
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Round names are great but not required.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            A reference to Project+ in the title is helpful but again optional. E.g. P+, Project+, Project Plus
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Some sort of symbol to separate the metadata such as a hyphen or bracket.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <span>Example Formatting:
                            <ul>
                            <br>
                                <li>
                                    <b>Event Name - Round - Player 1 (Character 1) vs. Player 2 (Character 2) - Project+</b>
                                </li>
                                <br>
                            </ul>
                            </span>
                        </b>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    A single large VOD with a description containing timestamps, player names and respective characters.
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Example of needed metadata: <b>00:00 Player 1 (Falco) vs. Player 2 (Marth)</b>, one match per line.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <br>
    <li>
        You can also volunteer to add VODS yourself via our <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1kKvNCndcfb4ePEtqtyjCbqHNPnTq1kxkUaZtPF1YOAM/edit?gid=1869225218#gid=1869225218" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Sheet.</a>

        <ul>
        <br>
            <li>
                If you are interested in doing so, please do one of the following to gain access to the sheet:
            </li>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Request access to the sheet via the link above and include some information about yourself.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Create an <a href="https://github.com/WhiteTPoison/projectplusvods/issues/new">issue</a> on GitHub.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </ul>
        <ul>
        <br>
            <li>
                <u><b>Sheet format</b></u> (one row per match):
            </li>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Columns, in order: <b>URL</b>, <b>Player 1</b>, <b>Character 1</b>, <b>Player 2</b>, <b>Character 2</b>, <b>Event Name</b>, <b>Round</b> (optional), <b>Date</b> (YYYY-MM-DD).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Multiple characters:</b> if a player used more than one character in the set, put all of them in that player's character cell, separated by a comma, e.g. <b>Fox, Falco</b>.
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            List them in the order they were played; the site shows each character's icon side by side in that order.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            A slash also works (<b>Fox/Falco</b>). Names with an "&amp;" such as <b>Mr. Game &amp; Watch</b> count as one character.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Searching for any of a player's characters will find the match.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    Use the character's full name (e.g. <b>Captain Falcon</b>, <b>Zero Suit Samus</b>); common short forms like Falcon, ZSS, D3 or ICs also work. Use <b>Random</b> if a character is unknown.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>
